<title>FRANCE: Seven French cabinet ministers lose jobs and seats.</title>
<headline>Seven French cabinet ministers lose jobs and seats.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Seven members of France's outgoing centre-right cabinet also lost their parliamentary seats as the country's left-wing coalition swept to a stunning general election victory on Sunday.</p>
<p>The seven ministers defeated in their home constituencies were:</p>
<p>- Justice Minister Jacques Toubon</p>
<p>- Budget Minister Alain Lamassoure</p>
<p>- Integration Minister Eric Raoult</p>
<p>- Housing Minister Pierre-Andre Perissol</p>
<p>- Overseas Territories Minister Jean-Jacques de Peretti</p>
<p>- Employment Minister Anne-Marie Couderc</p>
<p>- Environment Minister Corinne Lepage</p>
